`cellAt` answers `Cell`, and `parallelFrom` hands back only a number, a `boolean`, an enum, a `string` or an array of numbers, booleans or enums, which the join copies out of the worker's arena: anything else would point into memory the worker frees or reuses; answer the number or string the caller needs, one result per field if it needs several, and build the object from them after the call, or run it on the thread that called it, `const cells: Cell[] = []; for (let i2 = 0; i2 < 3; i2++) { cells.push(cellAt(i2)) }`
